", "firstName": "Whitney", "initials": "W", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-4803-1992"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Radiological Sciences, David Geffen School of Medicine, University of California, Los Angeles, California , USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Weller M", "lastName": "Weller", "firstName": "Michael", "initials": "M", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-1748-174X"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Neurology, University Hospital and University of Zurich, Zurich, Switzerland."}]}}, {"fullName": "Tonn JC", "lastName": "Tonn", "firstName": "Jörg C", "initials": "JC", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Neurosurgery, Ludwig Maximilians-University of Munich, Munich, Germany."}, {"affiliation": "German Cancer Consortium, Partner Site Munich, Germany."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-1748-174X"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-9204-7038"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-0616-5706"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-1101-5075"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-3541-2315"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-4803-1992"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "5", "volume": "21", "journalIssueId": 2813688, "dateOfPublication": "2019 May", "monthOfPublication": 5, "yearOfPublication": 2019, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Neuro Oncol", "title": "Neuro-oncology", "essn": "1523-5866", "issn": "1522-8517", "nlmid": "100887420", "isoabbreviation": "Neuro Oncol"}, "printPublicationDate": "2019-05-01"}, "pubYear": "2019", "pageInfo": "585-595", "abstractText": "Brain metastases (BM) from extracranial cancer are associated with significant morbidity and mortality. Effective local treatment options are stereotactic radiotherapy, including radiosurgery or fractionated external beam radiotherapy, and surgical resection. The use of systemic treatment for intracranial disease control also is improving. BM diagnosis, treatment planning, and follow-up is most often based on contrast-enhanced magnetic resonance imaging (MRI). However, anatomic imaging modalities including standard MRI have limitations in accurately characterizing posttherapeutic reactive changes and treatment response. Molecular imaging techniques such as positron emission tomography (PET) characterize specific metabolic and cellular features of metastases, potentially providing clinically relevant information supplementing anatomic MRI. Here, the Response Assessment in Neuro-Oncology working group provides recommendations for the use of PET imaging in the clinical management of patients with BM based on evidence from studies validated by histology and/or clinical outcome.", "affiliation": "Department of Neurology, University Hospital Cologne, Cologne, Germany.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["review-article", "Review", "Journal Article"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "P50 CA211015", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Animals"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Brain Neoplasms", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "DG", "qualifierName": "diagnostic imaging"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "ME", "qualifierName": "metabolism"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "SC", "qualifierName": "secondary"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "TH", "qualifierName": "therapy"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Radiopharmaceuticals", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "ME", "qualifierName": "metabolism"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Positron-Emission Tomography", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "MT", "qualifierName": "methods"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Molecular Imaging", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "MT", "qualifierName": "methods"}]}}]}, "keywordList": {"keyword": ["Brain metastases", "Fet", "Fdg Pet", "Pseudoprogression", "Amino Acid Pet"]}, "chemicalList": {"chemical": [{"name": "Radiopharmaceuticals", "registryNumber": "0"}]}, "subsetList": {"subset": [{"code": "IM", "name": "Index Medicus"}]}, "fullTextUrlList": {"fullTextUrl": [{"availability": "Subscription required", "availabilityCode": "S", "documentStyle": "doi", "site": "DOI", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1093/neuonc/noz003"}, {"availability": "Free", "availabilityCode": "F", "documentStyle": "html", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC6502495"}, {"availability": "Free", "availabilityCode": "F", "documentStyle": "pdf", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC6502495?pdf=render"}, {"availability": "Free", "availabilityCode": "F", "documentStyle": "doi", "site": "DOI", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1093/neuonc/noz003"}]}, "isOpenAccess": "N", "inEPMC": "Y", "inPMC": "Y", "citedByCount": 147, "hasReferences": "Y", "hasTextMinedTerms": "Y", "hasDbCrossReferences": "N", "hasPDF": "Y", "hasBook": "N", "hasSuppl": "N", "hasLabsLinks": "Y", "hasData": "Y", "authMan": "N", "epmcAuthMan": "N", "nihAuthMan": "N", "hasTMAccessionNumbers": "Y", "tmAccessionTypeList": {"accessionType": ["doi"]}, "dateOfCompletion": "2020-08-19", "dateOfCreation": "2019-01-08", "dateOfRevision": "2020-08-27", "firstPublicationDate": "2019-05-01", "firstIndexDate": "2019-01-07", "fullTextReceivedDate": "2025-02-03", "embargoDate": "2020-05-01", "hasEvaluations": "N"}]}}